## Next.js App Router Delegation (`src/app/`)
Next.js App Router route handlers in `src/app/` act as thin route wrappers delegating directly to module page re-exports from `@/modules/<feature>`:
- `src/app/page.tsx` -> renders `HomePage` from `@/modules/home`
- `src/app/services/page.tsx` -> renders `ServicesPage` from `@/modules/services`
- `src/app/solutions/page.tsx` -> renders `SolutionsPage` from `@/modules/solutions`
- `src/app/technologies/page.tsx` -> renders `TechnologiesPage` from `@/modules/technologies`
- `src/app/projects/page.tsx` -> renders `ProjectsPage` from `@/modules/projects`
- `src/app/projects/[id]/page.tsx` -> renders `ProjectDetailPage` from `@/modules/projects`
- `src/app/process/page.tsx` -> renders `ProcessPage` from `@/modules/process`
- `src/app/industries/page.tsx` -> renders `IndustriesPage` from `@/modules/industries`
- `src/app/about/page.tsx` -> renders `AboutPage` from `@/modules/about`
- `src/app/contact/page.tsx` -> renders `ContactPage` from `@/modules/contact`

